*begin TBR
*export G2.001 TubularBore.pt3.068

;Cave:	Keld Head - Marble Steps Branch

*equate G2.020 ContinentalDrift.020
*equate ContinentalDrift.024 TubularBore.pt1.024

;G2 Passage: 26-4-10
;Continental Drift: 6-5-10
;Tubular Bore: 6-5-10 (to 660 m), 12-06-10 (660 m to 805 m), 28-6-10 (805 m to the end at 923 m, where it joins the original route to this point via Great Western).

;Lengths given are calculated for 020 and 024. Somewhere before 660m junction an extra metre appears in the calc. lengths, so each stn is 1 metre further into the dive than the distances given in the notes (Footleg, June 2013)

*begin G2
	*export 001 020
	*date 2010.04.26
	*calibrate declination +2.59

	*data diving from to bearing length fromdepth todepth
	001	002	55.0	2.50	-7.2	-7.3	;Start G2 001=450m
